### 5.3 Portal (frontend)

```javascript
// Status drives the button: authenticated=false → consent needed, true → linked.
const st = await api(`/v1/external-auth/primary-gitlab?plane=a`);

// Consent runs in the same tab so the flow ends back on the portal (?linked=1).
async function openViaBounce(body, { sameTab = false } = {}) {
  const w = sameTab ? window : window.open("about:blank", "_blank"); // open sync (popup blockers)
  if (!sameTab) w.opener = null;
  const data = await api("/v1/bounce/start", { method: "POST", body: JSON.stringify(body) });
  const form = w.document.createElement("form");
  form.method = "POST";                              // keeps the code out of URLs/logs
  form.action = data.bounce_url;                     // https://coder-a.example.com/_portal/bounce
  const input = w.document.createElement("input");
  input.type = "hidden"; input.name = "code"; input.value = data.code;
  form.appendChild(input);
  w.document.body.appendChild(form);
  form.submit();
}

openViaBounce({ plane: "a", purpose: "external-auth", provider: "primary-gitlab" }, { sameTab: true });
// Unlink:
api(`/v1/external-auth/primary-gitlab?plane=a`, { method: "DELETE" });
```

### 5.4 Middle — start (user-authenticated)

```go
// POST /v1/bounce/start — redirect computed server-side, never from the client
case "external-auth":
    redirect = "/external-auth/" + in.Provider + "/callback?redirect=" + url.QueryEscape(cfg.Bounce.DonePath)
case "terminal":
    redirect = fmt.Sprintf("/@%s/%s.%s/terminal", user, workspace, agent)
code, _ := s.Bounce.Issue(bounceCode{Email: email, Plane: p.ID, Redirect: redirect, Purpose: in.Purpose, Exp: now.Add(60 * time.Second)})
writeJSON(w, 200, map[string]any{"bounce_url": p.URL + "/_portal/bounce", "code": code})
```

`/callback` without `?code` makes Coder start the provider redirect immediately (skips Coder's
"Login with GitLab" page); `?redirect=` is remembered in Coder's `oauth_redirect` cookie and used
after the link is stored.

### 5.5 Middle — redeem and done (IAM-authenticated)

```go
// POST /internal/bounce/redeem
plane, arn, err := s.verifyBounceCaller(ctx, in.IAM, "redeem", in.Code) // STS replay + allowlist
rec, ok := s.Bounce.Consume(in.Code)                                     // single use
// rec.Plane == plane && host == plane host, then:
if rec.Purpose == "external-auth" {
    tok = mint "bounce-<plane>" key, lifetime 300s                       // revoked at /done
} else {
    tok = main "middle-<plane>" key
}
writeJSON(w, 200, map[string]any{"session_token": tok, "redirect_path": rec.Redirect, "max_age": maxAge})

// POST /internal/bounce/done
plane, arn, err := s.verifyBounceCaller(ctx, in.IAM, "done", in.SessionToken)
// host == plane host; GetMe(token) → user; delete the key whose id == token prefix
// AND name == "bounce-<plane>"; always answer with the portal URL
writeJSON(w, 200, map[string]any{"redirect_url": cfg.Bounce.DoneRedirect, "revoked": revoked})
```

`verifyBounceCaller` requires: `x-middle-server-id` == `bounce.server_id`, `x-middle-code-sha256`
== sha256(action + "\n" + value), both listed in `SignedHeaders`, body exactly
`Action=GetCallerIdentity&Version=2011-06-15`, then POSTs to the configured STS endpoint only.

### 5.6 Lambda — two paths

```go
func (h *Handler) Handle(ctx context.Context, ev events.ALBTargetGroupRequest) (events.ALBTargetGroupResponse, error) {
    if strings.HasSuffix(ev.Path, "/done") {
        return h.done(ctx, ev) // cookie → middle /internal/bounce/done → 302 portal + clear cookie
    }
    // code (form POST) → middle /internal/bounce/redeem → 302 redirect_path + Set-Cookie
}

// Identity proof (built, never sent by the Lambda):
req, _ := http.NewRequest("POST", "https://sts.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/", strings.NewReader(stsBody))
req.Header.Set("Content-Type", "application/x-www-form-urlencoded; charset=utf-8")
req.Header.Set("X-Middle-Server-Id", serverID)
req.Header.Set("X-Middle-Code-Sha256", hex(sha256(action + "\n" + value)))
v4.NewSigner().SignHTTP(ctx, creds, req, bodyHash, "sts", "us-east-1", time.Now())
```

Responses:

```text
redeem: 302 Location: /external-auth/primary-gitlab/callback?redirect=%2F_portal%2Fdone
        Set-Cookie: coder_session_token=…; Path=/; Max-Age=300; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax
done:   302 Location: https://portal.example.com/?linked=1
        Set-Cookie: coder_session_token=; Path=/; Max-Age=0; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax
both:   Cache-Control: no-store, Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
```

Lambda env: `MIDDLE_URL`, `MIDDLE_SERVER_ID`, `STS_REGION`, `COOKIE_SECURE=true`.
Build: `GOOS=linux GOARCH=arm64 go build -tags lambda.norpc -o bootstrap ./cmd/lambda`.

### 5.7 ALB (per plane)

```text
HTTPS listener (cert covers coder-a.example.com and *.coder-a.example.com)
  priority 10: host = coder-a.example.com AND path = /_portal/*  → Lambda target group (bounce-plane-a)
  default / lower priority: coder-a.example.com, *.coder-a.example.com → coderd
```

One rule covers both `/_portal/bounce` and `/_portal/done`.

EKS / AWS Load Balancer Controller equivalent: an Ingress in the **same IngressGroup** as Coder's
with a lower `alb.ingress.kubernetes.io/group.order`, whose `/_portal/` path uses a custom action
(`alb.ingress.kubernetes.io/actions.bounce` with `forwardConfig.targetGroups[].targetGroupARN`)
pointing at a Lambda target group created outside the controller (Terraform `aws_lb_target_group`
`target_type = "lambda"` + `aws_lambda_permission` for `elasticloadbalancing.amazonaws.com`).
Alternatively manage just this rule in Terraform with `aws_lb_listener_rule`.

## 6. Networking options for Lambda → middle

| Option | When |
| --- | --- |
| Public `https://middle.example.com` | Middle is internet-reachable (lab used private because the ALB was IP-restricted) |
| **Lambda in VPC → private middle URL** (used in AWS lab) | Middle in same/peered VPC; no NAT needed (signing is local, middle calls STS) |
| Lambda in VPC → internal NLB in front of middle | Middle elsewhere over TGW/VPN/DX with stable private IPs |

The IAM check is identical in all cases.

## 7. Way forward

### Adopt

1. **One bounce Lambda + IAM role per plane** (`coder-bounce-<plane>`), trusted by middle via the
   allowlist. Role needs no permissions beyond Lambda basics (+ VPC access if in VPC).
2. **One ALB rule per plane host** (`/_portal/*`, highest priority), matching the exact plane
   host — not the wildcard app hosts.
3. **GitLab OAuth** through the bounce with the `/done` cleanup:
   - portal shows status from `GET /v1/external-auth/{id}?plane=` (`authenticated`);
   - "Connect GitLab" = `purpose: "external-auth"` in the same tab; the flow ends on the portal;
   - consent uses a dedicated 5-minute `bounce-<plane>` key, revoked at `/_portal/done`;
   - one GitLab OAuth app (redirect URI) per plane host.
4. **Apps / ttyd**: keep the JSON mint + strip flow ([`open-coder-apps-portal-json-strip.md`](open-coder-apps-portal-json-strip.md)).
5. **Built-in web terminal**: not needed when ttyd is used. If ever enabled, note that the
   `terminal` purpose leaves a dashboard-capable cookie on the plane host (by design: the terminal
   *is* a dashboard page) — either drop the purpose or give it the same dedicated short-lived key.

### Production hardening (not needed for the validation lab)

| Item | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Shared code store (Redis/DynamoDB TTL, atomic get-and-delete) | Multi-replica middle; exactly-once redeem |
| Serve `/internal/*` on a private listener / not via the public ALB | Defense in depth (IAM proof already required) |
| Pin `role_id` in the allowlist | Recreated role with same name isn't auto-trusted |
| Audit log on redeem/done (user, plane, purpose, caller ARN, revoked) | Traceability of cookie grants / GitLab linking |
| Periodic sweep of stale `bounce-<plane>` keys | Belt and braces for abandoned consents (they expire in 5 min anyway) |
| Rate-limit `/v1/bounce/start` per user | Code minting is cheap but should not be abusable |
| Alarm on `rejected caller` / STS failures | Detect misconfig or probing |
| GitLab app secret in a secret store, rotated | Coder reads it from env at start |

